My recollection of Section 504 of the Copyright Act is that the victim of
infringement can sue for lost profits, or elect to receive $500 to $20,000
per infringed-upon work (or up to $100,000 if the copyright owner proves
the infringement was willful).  Oh, and they can recover their attorney's
fees, too.  There's certainly no lack of incentive to go after solvent
parties that can afford that sort of thing, other than, maybe, bad publicity.
