that a student is discovered to be engaging in some flagrant abuse.  At
one point for instance I knew a student who was very fond of securing
the use of a workstation for his exclusive use by remotely running a program
whose sole purpose was to cause enormous amounts of paging.  (Many of
the students who were victims of this weren't sophisticated enough to
know more than that the workstation had suddenly become too sluggish to
use.  They would leave, thinking they might come back later.)  How do
you deal with this if you can't shut down this person's account
immediately?  How long can you let him go on inconveniencing his fellow
students?

