Suggestion: Open up the Scarborough Campus computers. Give them "nn" dollars
to play with. Set up a charging system, and charge students for going over
the limit. 

Suggestion (2):  Have the University open up an account where all students
can have access, if they want, by paying for it.

At UBC (I was at UToronto), we get 20 minutes free/day of access and are
allowed (Actually encouraged) to use EMail, UseNet. We are put into a Gopher
Shell and are basically allowed to access anywhere in the world via Gopher,
if we know what we're doing.

After the 20 minutes are up, we pay 1.75 cents/per minute for off-campus
dialin time (all speeds) and certain disk usage and disk storage charges.

With this funding that the University receives from people like me, they
are able to provide more services to students without the "Draconian" mea-
sures that are in place at Scarborough.

Even as a graduate school, we sometimes have limits on our funding. For
example, I am being given $20 onto my account to complete a small computer
project for one of our classes. If I use the $$$ to download pictures of Elle
MacPherson or whether I use it to do this project is completely up to me. 
It's my responsibility.

So, inotherwords, make the students responsible for themselves rather than
have an ominous overseer seemingly watching everything they do.

